Descriptive Statistics Using Scala Collections

Aim:

1.Create a list of numbers.
2.Calculate mean, median, and mode using Scala collections.
3.Display the results in formatted output.

Code:-

object Main {
  def main(args: Array[String]): Unit = {

    // Create a list of numbers
    val numbers = List(12, 15, 18, 20, 15, 22, 18, 15, 25, 30)

    // Mean
    val mean = numbers.sum.toDouble / numbers.length

    // Median
    val sorted = numbers.sorted
    val n = sorted.length

    val median =
      if (n % 2 == 0)
        (sorted(n / 2 - 1) + sorted(n / 2)) / 2.0
      else
        sorted(n / 2)

    // Mode
    val mode = numbers
      .groupBy(identity)
      .map { case (num, list) => (num, list.size) }
      .maxBy(_._2)
      ._1

    // Display results
    println("================================")
    println("       Statistical Analysis")
    println("================================")
    println("Numbers: " + numbers.mkString(", "))
    println(f"Mean:   $mean%.2f")
    println(f"Median: $median%.2f")
    println("Mode:   " + mode)
    println("================================")
  }
}

